nd is easy to draw from where the channel is open; in early season find a spot where the creek is running clear of snow", "permit": "This is the ambiguous one and it matters. The Stuart Lake trailhead sits inside the Enchantment Permit Area, and the Stuart Zone requires an overnight permit from May 15 through October 31, drawn either through the February advance lottery on the federal reservation system or through the daily lottery run from Leavenworth. Where the zone boundary falls in the upper Mountaineer Creek basin above the lakes is not clearly drawn on any public map, and reasonable people read it differently. Do not guess. Call the Wenatchee River Ranger District before the trip, and if you cannot get an answer, carry a Stuart Zone permit. Day use anywhere in the permit area needs only the free self-issued slip at the trailhead. Dogs are prohibited throughout the permit area and campfires are banned.", "capacity": "Plenty of good spots spread along the bench near the creek; several parties can spread out without seeing each other"}]'::jsonb WHERE id = 'wa_sherpa_peak_east_ridge';

-- wa_sherpa_peak_west_ridge: bivy pruned 4->3, removing one leftover foreign-peak entry ('Beverly and De Roux campgrounds and the North Fork Teanaway roadside camps', explicitly for Ingalls Peak: 'This is what most parties on Ingalls Peak actually use') that survived an earlier, partial cleanup of this row's bivy list (its gain_ft/loss_ft were already synced 2026-07-31, but the bivy array itself still carried this one foreign entry). The three remaining entries all explicitly name Sherpa Peak.
